  "body": "  Shown below are three augmented matrices in reduced row echelon form. For each matrix, identify the pivot positions and describe the solution space in parametric form (if any solutions exist).             There are three pivots located in the 1st row and 1st column, 2nd row and 2nd column, and 3rd row and 3rd column. See bold blue entries above. The solution in parametric form is , , and . This means that there is one unique solution of .              There are two pivots located in the 1st row and 1st column and 2nd row and 2nd column. See bold blue entries above. Reading from the matrix, we have the following system of equations: where is free since there is no pivot in the column corresponding to that variable. Writing these equations in parametric form we then have: and . Due to being free, this system of equations has infinitely many solutions.              There are three pivots located in the 1st row and 1st column, 2nd row and 2nd column and 3rd row and 4th column. See bold blue entries above. This system has no solutions due to the third row, which has a pivot in the rightmost column of the augmented matrix. This third row yields the equation , which is not mathematically possible. Therefore, there are no solutions.    "
