  "body": "  Let's put some more technical terms to the magic carpet\/hoverboard scenario. Recall the following movement:   You and your cousin's hoverboard travel in the direction .    Your magic carpet can move in the direction .    Your cousin's magic carpet can move in the direction .        Describe the set of vectors that result from linear combinations of and .    All of .      Describe the set of vectors that result from linear combinations of and .    A line, with the slope 1\/3, going through the origin.      What is Span ? Try to describe geometrically and algebraically.    Geometrically, this is all of . Algebraically, this is for any real number .      What is Span ? Try to describe geometrically and algebraically.    Geometrically, this is a line. Algebraically, this is for any real number . Note, that we don't need the because it is a scalar multiple of .      For what vectors does the matrix equation have a solution?    All vectors in .      For what vectors does the matrix equation have a solution?    All vectors for any value (a line).      How many pivots does the matrix have? How might this be related to your answer for Span ?    The row reduced echelon form of is the identity matrix, which means that the system is always consistent, no matter what is. There is a pivot in every row!      How many pivots does the matrix have? How might this be related to your answer for Span ?    The row reduced echelon form of is , which means that there is only 1 pivot and thus, not always a solution. For some there could be a pivot in the rightmost column of the augmented matrix for the corresponding linear system, thus resulting in no solution.    "
