  "body": "  Last class we looked at the transition matrix applied to trucks at two locations. We wanted to know the long-term behavior of an initial state that evolves as . In other words, what happened to as grows large. We found that had eigenvalues and , and the . So if we start with 1000 trucks total so that , then in the long-term we have so there will be 750 trucks at location and 250 at location .  Let's look at a different transition matrix: .     Find the eigenvalues of and bases for its eigenspaces.      Find a diagonalization of .      What happens when you look at as grows?      What is different about the eigenvalues of and that distinguishes the long-term behavior?    "
